IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc25-remediation-approval`

-- ccc25-tests-remediation-approval.l4 -- tests for sections 715.36 to 715.43 (src lines 14954 to 15033).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, with the words that decide it.

§ `Section 715.36 -- informing victims`
-- 14954 (1): After an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice, the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim. Argument: the organization has accepted.
#ASSERT `s 715.36(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim, or any third party acting on the victim’s behalf, that a remediation agreement may be entered into` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after the organization has accepted the offer
#ASSERT `s 715.36(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim, or any third party acting on the victim’s behalf, that a remediation agreement may be entered into` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "After": before acceptance the duty has not arisen (a gate in the text's words)
-- 14956 (2): the duty is to be construed and applied in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances and not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice, including by causing interference with prosecutorial discretion or compromising, hindering or causing excessive delay.
-- Field order: reasonable in the circumstances; interferes with the proper administration of justice; interferes with prosecutorial discretion; compromises the negotiation or its conclusion; hinders it; causes excessive delay to it.
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- reasonable, and none of the interferences
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not reasonable in the circumstances
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- likely to interfere: the proper administration of justice
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- likely to interfere: prosecutorial discretion
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- likely to interfere: compromising the negotiation
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- likely to interfere: hindering the negotiation
#ASSERT `s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` (`s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- likely to interfere: excessive delay
-- 14958 (3): If the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1), they must provide the court ... with a statement of the reasons. Argument: the prosecutor so elects.
#ASSERT `s 715.36(3) the prosecutor must provide the court with a statement of the reasons why it was not appropriate to inform` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- elects not to inform
#ASSERT `s 715.36(3) the prosecutor must provide the court with a statement of the reasons why it was not appropriate to inform` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty arises only on the text's "If"

§ `Section 715.37 -- application for approval`
-- 14960 (1): When the prosecutor and the organization have agreed to the terms of a remediation agreement, the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the terms are agreed
#ASSERT `s 715.37(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "When": no agreement on terms yet, the duty has not arisen
-- 14962 (2): The coming into force of the agreement is subject to the approval of the court.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(2) the court’s approval, to which the coming into force of the agreement is subject, has been given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- approved
#ASSERT `s 715.37(2) the court’s approval, to which the coming into force of the agreement is subject, has been given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not approved: the condition of coming into force is not met
-- 14964-14968 (3): the court must consider (a) the reparations, statement and measures of 715.34(1)(g); (b) the prosecutor's statement under 715.36(3); (c) any victim or community impact statement; (d) any victim surcharge under 715.34(1)(h).
#ASSERT `s 715.37(3) the court must consider the matter in determining whether to approve the agreement` `s 715.37(3)(a) any reparations, statement and other measure referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(g)` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed matter (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(3) the court must consider the matter in determining whether to approve the agreement` `s 715.37(3)(b) any statement made by the prosecutor under subsection 715.36(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed matter (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(3) the court must consider the matter in determining whether to approve the agreement` `s 715.37(3)(c) any victim or community impact statement presented to the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed matter (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(3) the court must consider the matter in determining whether to approve the agreement` `s 715.37(3)(d) any victim surcharge referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(h)` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed matter (d)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(3) the court must consider the matter in determining whether to approve the agreement` `s 715.37(3) a matter that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other matter: not covered
-- 14970 (4): the rules provided for in sections 722 to 722.2 apply, other than subsection 722(6). Argument: the provision (section as a decimal, subsection).
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 722
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "(2)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- subsection 722(2) is within section 722 and is not 722(6)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722.1, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 722.1
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722.2, "(5)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- subsection 722.2(5)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722, "(6)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- other than subsection 722(6): the text says no
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 721, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 721 is outside sections 722 to 722.2
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 723, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 723 is outside sections 722 to 722.2
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 722.3, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- a section number past 722.2 is outside the range
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4) the rules in the provision apply for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 721.9, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- a section number before 722 is outside the range
-- 14971 (4)(a): a victim or community impact statement, or any other evidence concerning any victim, must be considered when determining whether to approve the agreement.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(a) the court must consider the statement or evidence when determining whether to approve the agreement under subsection (6)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a victim impact statement or other evidence concerning a victim
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(a) the court must consider the statement or evidence when determining whether to approve the agreement under subsection (6)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other material: outside the paragraph
-- 14972 (4)(b): the inquiry referred to in subsection 722(2) must be made at the hearing of the application. Arguments: it is that inquiry; it is made at the hearing.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(b) the inquiry referred to in subsection 722(2) is made at the hearing of the application, as required` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- that inquiry, at the hearing
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(b) the inquiry referred to in subsection 722(2) is made at the hearing of the application, as required` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- that inquiry, not at the hearing: the text says it must be made at the hearing
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(b) the inquiry referred to in subsection 722(2) is made at the hearing of the application, as required` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different inquiry: outside the paragraph
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(b) the inquiry referred to in subsection 722(2) is made at the hearing of the application, as required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different inquiry: outside the paragraph
-- 14973 (4)(c): the duty of the clerk under section 722.1 or subsection 722.2(5) is deemed to be the duty of the prosecutor.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(c) the duty of the clerk is deemed to be the duty of the prosecutor to make reasonable efforts to provide a copy of the statement to the organization or counsel for the organization` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the clerk's duty under 722.1 or 722.2(5)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(4)(c) the duty of the clerk is deemed to be the duty of the prosecutor to make reasonable efforts to provide a copy of the statement to the organization or counsel for the organization` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another duty of the clerk: outside the paragraph
-- 14975 (5): the amount of the victim surcharge is 30% of any penalty referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(f), or any other percentage that the prosecutor deems appropriate. Arguments: the penalty in dollars; the other percentage if the prosecutor deems one appropriate; the offence is under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the amount of the victim surcharge in dollars` 1000 NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST 300   -- 30% of 1000 is 300
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the amount of the victim surcharge in dollars` 1000 (JUST 50) FALSE EQUALS JUST 500   -- another percentage the prosecutor deems appropriate: 50% of 1000
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the amount of the victim surcharge in dollars` 200 (JUST 10) FALSE EQUALS JUST 20   -- 10% of 200
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the amount of the victim surcharge in dollars` 0 NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST 0   -- 30% of nothing
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the amount of the victim surcharge in dollars` 1000 NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a section 3 or 4 offence of that Act has no surcharge under paragraph 715.34(1)(h): not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the victim surcharge is payable to the treasurer of the province in which the application for approval is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- payable to the treasurer of the province of the application
#ASSERT `s 715.37(5) the victim surcharge is payable to the treasurer of the province in which the application for approval is made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made in a province: not covered
-- 14977-14980 (6): the court must, by order, approve the agreement if it is satisfied that (a) the organization is charged with an offence to which the agreement applies; (b) the agreement is in the public interest; and (c) the terms are fair, reasonable and proportionate to the gravity of the offence.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(6) the court must, by order, approve the agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- satisfied of all three
#ASSERT `s 715.37(6) the court must, by order, approve the agreement` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(6) the court must, by order, approve the agreement` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.37(6) the court must, by order, approve the agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of (c)
-- 14982 (7): As soon as practicable after the court approves the agreement, the prosecutor must direct the clerk ... to make an entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed. Argument: the court has approved.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(7) the prosecutor must direct the clerk or other proper officer of the court to make an entry on the record` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after the court approves
#ASSERT `s 715.37(7) the prosecutor must direct the clerk or other proper officer of the court to make an entry on the record` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "after the court approves": not approved, the direction is not yet due
-- Arguments: the court has approved; the entry has been made; the offence is one to which the agreement applies.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(7) the proceedings against the organization in respect of the offence are stayed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- approved, entry made, the offence is covered
#ASSERT `s 715.37(7) the proceedings against the organization in respect of the offence are stayed` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not approved: no stay
#ASSERT `s 715.37(7) the proceedings against the organization in respect of the offence are stayed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no entry yet: the proceedings are stayed only once the entry is made
#ASSERT `s 715.37(7) the proceedings against the organization in respect of the offence are stayed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an offence to which the agreement does not apply: outside the subsection
-- 14984 (8): No other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence while the agreement is in force. Arguments: the agreement is in force; the proceedings are other proceedings against the organization for the same offence.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(8) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- in force, same offence: the bar applies
#ASSERT `s 715.37(8) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "while the agreement is in force": not in force, the bar does not apply
#ASSERT `s 715.37(8) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- different proceedings: outside the bar
-- 14986 (9): The running of a limitation period in respect of any offence to which the agreement applies is suspended while the agreement is in force.
#ASSERT `s 715.37(9) the running of the limitation period is suspended` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- in force, a limitation period for a covered offence
#ASSERT `s 715.37(9) the running of the limitation period is suspended` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in force: not suspended
#ASSERT `s 715.37(9) the running of the limitation period is suspended` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a limitation period for another offence: outside the subsection

§ `Sections 715.38 to 715.41 -- variation, termination, completion, the deadline`
-- 14988: On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, approve any modification if the court is satisfied that the agreement continues to meet the conditions set out in subsection 715.37(6). Arguments: the prosecutor applied; the three satisfactions.
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the court must, by order, approve the modification to the remediation agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- applied and satisfied of all three conditions
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the court must, by order, approve the modification to the remediation agreement` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the court must, by order, approve the modification to the remediation agreement` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the court must, by order, approve the modification to the remediation agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the court must, by order, approve the modification to the remediation agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of (c)
-- 14988: On approval, the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement.
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- approved
#ASSERT `s 715.38 the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not approved: not deemed part
-- 14990 (1): On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, terminate the agreement if it is satisfied that the organization has breached a term of the agreement. Arguments: applied; satisfied of a breach.
#ASSERT `s 715.39(1) the court must, by order, terminate the agreement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- applied and satisfied of a breach
#ASSERT `s 715.39(1) the court must, by order, terminate the agreement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application
#ASSERT `s 715.39(1) the court must, by order, terminate the agreement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of a breach
-- 14992 (2): As soon as the order is made, proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection 715.37(7) may be recommenced ... by the prosecutor giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk. Arguments: an order has been made under (1); the proceedings were stayed under 715.37(7).
#ASSERT `s 715.39(2) the stayed proceedings may be recommenced without a new information or a new indictment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- order made, proceedings so stayed
#ASSERT `s 715.39(2) the stayed proceedings may be recommenced without a new information or a new indictment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "As soon as the order is made": no order yet (an "upon"-kind gate: listed, JUST FALSE by the periods ruling)
#ASSERT `s 715.39(2) the stayed proceedings may be recommenced without a new information or a new indictment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- proceedings not stayed under 715.37(7): outside the subsection
-- 14994 (3): If no notice is given within one year after the order is made, or before the expiry of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is earlier, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced. Arguments: the day of the order; the day the time for commencing expires.
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the last day on which notice of recommencement can be given to the clerk` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027   -- the first anniversary of the order is earlier than the expiry of the time
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the last day on which notice of recommencement can be given to the clerk` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS Date 1 6 2026   -- the expiry of the time is earlier than the first anniversary
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the last day on which notice of recommencement can be given to the clerk` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027   -- both are the same day
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the last day on which notice of recommencement can be given to the clerk` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025   -- one year after 29 February 2024 is read as 28 February 2025 (fork F11: a year on is the same day, clamped)
-- Arguments: the day of the order; the day the time for commencing expires; the day notice was given (if it was); the day the question is asked.
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) (JUST (Date 15 3 2027)) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- notice given on the last day, which is within one year
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) (JUST (Date 14 9 2026)) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- notice given within the year
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) (JUST (Date 16 3 2027)) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- notice given a day after the year: not given within one year
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- notice given on the day the time expires
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (JUST (Date 2 6 2026)) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- notice given after the time for commencing expired, though within the year
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) NOTHING (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no notice and the year is over
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice yet but the last day is today: the period has not run out
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2030) NOTHING (Date 14 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice yet and the period has not run out
#ASSERT `s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) NOTHING (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no notice and the time for commencing has expired, which is earlier than the year
-- 14996 (1): On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met if it is satisfied that the organization has complied with the agreement. Arguments: applied; satisfied of compliance.
#ASSERT `s 715.4(1) the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- applied and satisfied of compliance
#ASSERT `s 715.4(1) the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application
#ASSERT `s 715.4(1) the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of compliance
-- 14998 (2): The order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced and no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence. Arguments: the effect; an order has been made under (1); the offence is one to which the agreement applies.
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) the order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named effect of the order
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) the order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order under (1): outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) the order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an offence to which the agreement applies: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named effect of the order
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order under (1): outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an offence to which the agreement applies: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named effect of the order
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order under (1): outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` `s 715.4(2) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an offence to which the agreement applies: outside the subsection
-- 15000 (1): The prosecutor must, as soon as practicable after the deadline referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(p), apply to the court in writing for a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline, an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39 or an order under section 715.4. Arguments: the deadline has passed; the order.
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` TRUE `s 715.41(1) a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after the deadline, a named order
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` FALSE `s 715.41(1) a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "after the deadline": the deadline has not passed
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` TRUE `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after the deadline, a named order
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` FALSE `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "after the deadline": the deadline has not passed
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` TRUE `s 715.41(1) an order under section 715.4 declaring that its terms were met` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after the deadline, a named order
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` FALSE `s 715.41(1) an order under section 715.4 declaring that its terms were met` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "after the deadline": the deadline has not passed
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` TRUE `s 715.41(1) an order that none of those names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another order: outside the section
-- 15000: ... and the court may issue any of these orders as it deems appropriate. Arguments: the prosecutor has applied for the order; the order; the court deems it appropriate.
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the court may issue the order as it deems appropriate` TRUE `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- applied for, a named order, the court deems it appropriate
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the court may issue the order as it deems appropriate` FALSE `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no application: the grant's gate fails, not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the court may issue the order as it deems appropriate` TRUE `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court does not deem it appropriate: the grant's gate fails, not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.41(1) the court may issue the order as it deems appropriate` TRUE `s 715.41(1) an order that none of those names` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another order: outside the section
-- 15002 (2): The agreement is deemed to remain in force until a court issues an order terminating it or declaring that its terms were met. Arguments: the agreement has come into force with the court's approval; a termination order has been issued; a declaration order has been issued.
#ASSERT `s 715.41(2) the agreement is deemed to remain in force` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before any order
#ASSERT `s 715.41(2) the agreement is deemed to remain in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until": after a termination order
#ASSERT `s 715.41(2) the agreement is deemed to remain in force` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until": after a declaration that the terms were met
#ASSERT `s 715.41(2) the agreement is deemed to remain in force` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an agreement that never came into force: outside the subsection

§ `Sections 715.42 and 715.43 -- publication, regulations, deletion of an offence`
-- 15004-15007 (1): Subject to subsection (2), the following must be published by the court as soon as practicable: (a) the agreement; (b) an order and reasons under 715.37 to 715.41; (c) a decision under (2) or (5) and its reasons. Arguments: the item; the court has decided under (2) not to publish it.
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1)(a) the remediation agreement approved by the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the agreement, no decision to withhold
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1)(a) the remediation agreement approved by the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Subject to subsection (2)": the court has decided not to publish the agreement
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1)(b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an order and reasons, no decision to withhold
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1)(b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Subject to subsection (2)": the court has decided not to publish it
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1)(c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a decision under (2) or (5): published
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1)(c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- subsection (2) lets the court withhold only the agreement and the orders and reasons of (1)(b), so a decision under (2) is still published
#ASSERT `s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` `s 715.42(1) an item that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an item the paragraphs do not name: not covered
-- 15009 (2): The court may decide not to publish the agreement or any order or reasons referred to in paragraph (1)(b), in whole or in part, if it is satisfied that the non-publication is necessary for the proper administration of justice. Arguments: the item; the court is satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` `s 715.42(1)(a) the remediation agreement approved by the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the agreement, and the court is satisfied
#ASSERT `s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` `s 715.42(1)(b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an order or reasons, and the court is satisfied
#ASSERT `s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` `s 715.42(1)(a) the remediation agreement approved by the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the grant's "if" gate fails: not covered, not "may not" (fork F2)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` `s 715.42(1)(b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the grant's "if" gate fails: not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` `s 715.42(1)(c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a decision under (2) or (5) is not among the things the court may withhold: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` `s 715.42(1) an item that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another item: outside the grant
-- 15011-15017 (3): the court must consider (a) to (f). Arguments: the factor; the court considers the factor relevant (read only for (f)).
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims in the criminal justice process` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed factor (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(b) whether it is necessary to protect the identity of any victims, any person not engaged in the wrongdoing and any person who brought the wrongdoing to the attention of investigative authorities` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed factor (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(c) the prevention of any adverse effect to any ongoing investigation or prosecution` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed factor (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(d) whether effective alternatives to the decision referred to in subsection (2) are available in the circumstances` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed factor (d)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(e) the salutary and deleterious effects of making the decision referred to in subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed factor (e)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(f) any other factor that the court considers relevant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- another factor the court considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` `s 715.42(3)(f) any other factor that the court considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a factor the court does not consider relevant: not covered
-- 15019 (4): The court may make its decision subject to any conditions that it considers appropriate, including a condition related to the duration of non-publication. Arguments: the court has made a decision under (2); the court considers the condition appropriate.
#ASSERT `s 715.42(4) the court may make its decision subject to the condition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a decision under (2) and the court considers the condition appropriate
#ASSERT `s 715.42(4) the court may make its decision subject to the condition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no decision under (2): outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.42(4) the court may make its decision subject to the condition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a condition the court does not consider appropriate: the grant's gate fails, not covered
-- 15021 (5): On application by any person, the court must review the decision made under subsection (2). Arguments: any person has applied; the decision was made under (2).
#ASSERT `s 715.42(5) the court must review the decision made under subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- application, a decision under (2)
#ASSERT `s 715.42(5) the court must review the decision made under subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "On application": no application, no duty
#ASSERT `s 715.42(5) the court must review the decision made under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a decision not made under (2): outside the subsection
-- 15021 (5): If the court is satisfied that the non-publication is no longer necessary, it must publish. Arguments: the court has reviewed the decision; the court is satisfied that non-publication is no longer necessary.
#ASSERT `s 715.42(5) the court must publish the agreement, order or reasons, in whole or in part, as soon as practicable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- reviewed and satisfied
#ASSERT `s 715.42(5) the court must publish the agreement, order or reasons, in whole or in part, as soon as practicable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no review yet: the duty has not arisen
#ASSERT `s 715.42(5) the court must publish the agreement, order or reasons, in whole or in part, as soon as practicable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied that non-publication is no longer necessary
-- 15033 (3): If the Governor in Council orders the deletion of an offence from the schedule, this Part continues to apply to an organization alleged to have committed that offence if a notice referred to in section 715.33 respecting that offence was sent to the organization before the day on which the order comes into force.
-- Arguments: the Governor in Council has ordered the deletion; the organization is alleged to have committed that offence; a notice was sent; the day it was sent; the day the order comes into force.
#ASSERT `s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- notice sent the day before the order comes into force
#ASSERT `s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- sent on the same day: not "before the day"
#ASSERT `s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 3 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- sent after the order came into force
#ASSERT `s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice was sent
#ASSERT `s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no deletion ordered: outside the subsection (fork F29)
#ASSERT `s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not alleged to have committed that offence: outside the subsection

§ `Regulative rules of sections 715.36 to 715.42, run with #TRACE`
-- Each trace is expected to end as the comment above it says. Where the text states no time limit the rule has no WITHIN, so an act not done leaves a standing obligation, never a breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.36(1) the prosecutor's duty to inform victims` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.36(1) take reasonable steps to inform any victim or third party` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.36(1) the prosecutor's duty to inform victims` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.36(3) the prosecutor's duty to give the court a statement of reasons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.36(3) provide the court with a statement of reasons` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.36(3) the prosecutor's duty to give the court a statement of reasons` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.37(1) the prosecutor's duty to apply for approval` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.37(1) apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(1) the prosecutor's duty to apply for approval` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.37(3) the court's duty to consider the matters` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.37(3) consider the matters` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(3) the court's duty to consider the matters` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.37(4)(a) the court's duty to consider the statement or evidence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.37(4)(a) consider the victim or community impact statement or other evidence concerning any victim` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(4)(a) the court's duty to consider the statement or evidence` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.37(4)(c) the prosecutor's deemed duty to provide a copy of the statement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.37(4)(c) make reasonable efforts to provide a copy of the statement to the organization or counsel for the organization` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(4)(c) the prosecutor's deemed duty to provide a copy of the statement` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.37(6) the court's duty to approve the agreement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.37(6) approve the agreement by order` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(6) the court's duty to approve the agreement` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.38 the court's duty to approve the modification` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.38 approve the modification by order` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.38 the court's duty to approve the modification` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.39(1) the court's duty to terminate the agreement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.39(1) terminate the agreement by order` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.39(1) the court's duty to terminate the agreement` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.4(1) the court's duty to declare that the terms were met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.4(1) declare by order that the terms of the agreement were met` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
