-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the permission is used)
#TRACE `s 715.39(2) the prosecutor's permission to recommence the proceedings by notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.39(2) give notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (a permission not used stays open)
#TRACE `s 715.39(2) the prosecutor's permission to recommence the proceedings by notice` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the permission is used)
#TRACE `s 715.42(2) the court's permission not to publish` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.42(2) decide not to publish` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (a permission not used stays open)
#TRACE `s 715.42(2) the court's permission not to publish` AT 0 WITH

-- 14982 (7): the prosecutor directs the clerk, and the entry must be made immediately (read as WITHIN 0 from the direction: fork F9).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (direction and entry at the same time)
#TRACE `s 715.37(7) the prosecutor's duty to direct the entry and the clerk's duty to make it immediately` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.37(7) direct the clerk or other proper officer to make an entry on the record` AT 3
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 715.37(7) make the entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed` AT 3

-- EXPECT BREACHED   (the entry came after the direction, so it was not immediate)
#TRACE `s 715.37(7) the prosecutor's duty to direct the entry and the clerk's duty to make it immediately` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.37(7) direct the clerk or other proper officer to make an entry on the record` AT 3
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 715.37(7) make the entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed` AT 4

-- EXPECT STANDING   (the direction is given and no later event shows the entry missed: the clerk's duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(7) the prosecutor's duty to direct the entry and the clerk's duty to make it immediately` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.37(7) direct the clerk or other proper officer to make an entry on the record` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (nothing yet: the prosecutor's duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.37(7) the prosecutor's duty to direct the entry and the clerk's duty to make it immediately` AT 0 WITH

